title: "pallet-xcm: make claiming trapped assets all-or-nothing"
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `pallet-xcm`'s `ClaimAssets` implementation now mints every claimed asset before consuming
      the asset trap. If any asset fails to mint, for example because the asset transactor no
      longer matches it, the claim fails (`ClaimAsset` errors with `UnknownClaim`) and the trap
      is left untouched so it can be claimed later. Previously the trap was consumed first and
      assets that failed to mint were skipped, so the claim succeeded with only part of the
      trapped assets.

      Fungible imbalances of assets minted before the failure are forgotten, mirroring
      `drop_assets`, so total issuance stays consistent even when the executor is configured with
      a non-transactional `TransactionalProcessor`.
  - audience: Runtime User
    description: |
      Claiming trapped assets, either with the `claim_assets` extrinsic or the `ClaimAsset` XCM
      instruction, now either returns all of the trapped assets or fails without consuming the
      trap.

crates:
  - name: pallet-xcm
    bump: patch
